{"type":"standard","title":"Denaʼina language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Denaʼina language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q27785","titles":{"canonical":"Denaʼina_language","normalized":"Denaʼina language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Denaʼina language</span></span>"},"pageid":413459,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Early_Indian_Languages_Alaska.jpg/330px-Early_Indian_Languages_Alaska.jpg","width":330,"height":416},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/Early_Indian_Languages_Alaska.jpg","width":1920,"height":2421},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1353123177","tid":"106d3f20-4abf-11f1-a995-8f1fb1572789","timestamp":"2026-05-08T09:19:50Z","description":"Athabaskan language of Alaska","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dena%CA%BCina_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dena%CA%BCina_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dena%CA%BCina_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Dena%CA%BCina_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dena%CA%BCina_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Dena%CA%BCina_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dena%CA%BCina_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Dena%CA%BCina_language"}},"extract":"Denaʼina, is the Athabaskan language of the region surrounding Cook Inlet. It is geographically unique in Alaska as the only Alaska Athabaskan language to include territory which borders salt water. Of the total Denaʼina population of about 900 people, only 75–95 members still speak Denaʼina.","extract_html":"<p><b>Denaʼina</b>, is the Athabaskan language of the region surrounding Cook Inlet. It is geographically unique in Alaska as the only Alaska Athabaskan language to include territory which borders salt water. Of the total Denaʼina population of about 900 people, only 75–95 members still speak Denaʼina.</p>"}